// Import modeling — dependency declarations between modules.
//
// An import is a reference from one scope to another scope's names.
// It is structurally distinct from items (content declarations):
//   - Items define new structure (types, functions, services)
//   - Imports reference existing structure from other modules
//
// Import representation on a module Node:
//   - Module items live in `children`
//   - Module imports live in `params` (unused by modules for type params)
//   - Each import node has: name = module path, children = specific names
//   - Wildcard import: children is empty (imports all exported names)
//   - Specific import: children are the imported name nodes
//
// This separation eliminates the need for metadata markers (__is_import,
// __import_all) — the structural position (params vs children) IS the
// distinction.

module std.import
